# KlassApp — Frontend Conventions

## ds-* Pattern Library

The project uses a `ds-*` CSS class convention for dashboard components:

| Pattern | Purpose | Examples |
|---|---|---|
| `ds-kpi-card` | KPI metric card (icon + value + label) | Student count, teacher count, fee totals |
| `ds-kpi-icon-wrap` | Icon container inside KPI card | Colored icon background |
| `ds-kpi-value` | Metric number text | Bold large font |
| `ds-kpi-label` | Metric description label | Muted small text |
| `ds-page-head` | Page header wrapper | Flex row with title + action button |
| `ds-page-head-title` | Page heading | `<h1>` styled |
| `ds-btn` | Base button | Shared button base styles |
| `ds-btn-primary` | Primary action button | Colored variant |
| `ds-btn-sm` | Small button size | Compact variant |

These are defined in `resources/assets/sass/` (custom SCSS). The original `@apply` directives that derived some of their values from Tailwind were replaced with hardcoded CSS in Phase 2b — changing Tailwind utility values will **not** automatically propagate to these selectors anymore. Stick to existing patterns rather than introducing new utility classes.

## Mobile-First Responsive Standards

- **Breakpoints tested**: 375px (small mobile), 414px (large mobile), 768px (tablet), 1280px+ (desktop)
- **Layout approach**: Stacked cards on mobile, multi-column on desktop — never horizontal scroll
- **Verification**: Confirm with real screenshots at each breakpoint, not computed CSS values
- **The project has had regressions from assuming CSS values match rendered output** — always render and capture visually

## Sidebar Convention (Option 3)

- Sidebar uses the established "Option 3" icon set
- Group hover-preview pattern on desktop (expands on hover over group indicator)
- Consistent with Pulse dashboard standard

## Tooling

- **Laravel Mix 4** (NOT Vite) — `npm run dev` / `npm run production`
- **Tailwind v4.3.3** — CSS-first config via `@theme` block in `resources/css/tailwind.css` (no `tailwind.config.js`). Uses PostCSS pipeline (`@tailwindcss/postcss` + `lightningcss`). The `@apply` directive uses no-dot syntax (`@apply text-sm`, not `@apply .text-sm`).
- **Vue 2.6.12** — Options API, `Vue.component()` registration, no `<script setup>`, no Composition API
- **Playwright** available in `node_modules` for E2E testing

## Migration Branch State (migration/tailwind4)

This branch has migrated from Tailwind v1.4.6 → v4.3.3. Key state differences from `main`:

### Layout Tailwind Source Matrix
Not all layouts load the same Tailwind source — **check which layout a page renders through before assuming a utility will work**:

| Layout | Tailwind source |
|---|---|
| `layouts/app.blade.php` | Local `tailwind.css` v4 build |
| `layouts/superadmin-app.blade.php` | Local `tailwind.css` v4 build |
| `layouts/admission.blade.php` | CDN v1.1.3 only — **no local v4 build** |
| `layouts/video.blade.php` | CDN v1.1.3 only — **no local v4 build** |
| `layouts/empty.blade.php` | ⛔ **None** — neither local nor CDN. First-priority unfixed blocker: wrapper flexbox utilities (`flex items-center justify-center min-h-screen`) are dead, auth pages render top-left. |
| `layouts/main.blade.php` | ⛔ **None** — neither local nor CDN. First-priority unfixed blocker: 35 marketing pages saturated with Tailwind utilities (`container mx-auto`, `bg-red-600`, `py-16`, `flex-grow`, etc.) are all dead. |
| `layouts/minimal.blade.php` | **None** — neither local nor CDN |

Landing pages (`landing.blade.php`, `landing2.blade.php`) use Tailwind Play CDN (browser JIT via `cdn.tailwindcss.com`) — self-configured, immune to the local migration.

### @Apply → Hardcoded CSS
The 31 `@apply` rules in `adminstyle.scss` / `style.scss` were replaced with hardcoded CSS values in Phase 2b because the PostCSS pipeline uses a separate entry file for `@import "tailwindcss"`, which sass-loader can't resolve. This means:
- Selectors like `.admin-h1`, `.tw-form-control`, `.submit-btn`, `.custom-table` are **plain CSS**, decoupled from Tailwind's utility system
- Changing Tailwind utilities will **not** propagate to these selectors automatically
- If editing these selectors, use raw CSS values (check `tailwindcss` v4 output or use `@apply` in the tailwind.css entry file instead)

### Regression Risk: Silent Property Drops
The Phase 2b `@apply`→CSS rewrite dropped unrecognized properties as `// UNKNOWN:` SCSS comments that never survived compilation. An exhaustive SCSS source sweep found **19 selectors across 21 lines** with dropped properties — all verified against the actual Tailwind v1.1.3 CDN file and fixed in commit `ef5bb77`. After the fix, zero `// UNKNOWN:` comments remain in the SCSS source. The compiled `app.css` was never the right place to check for these (SCSS strips line comments during compilation). This specific regression is resolved, but the pattern is worth knowing about: if any new `@apply`→CSS rewrites are done, the SCSS source must be inspected for dropped properties — the compiled CSS won't show them.

### v4 Preflight: Border Color Change
Tailwind v4 changed the default `border-color` from `#e2e8f0` (gray) to `currentColor`. Any bare `border` utility (without an explicit `border-*-color`) will render using the parent element's `color` instead of the expected light gray. This affects dividers (`border-r`, `border-b`, etc.) and card borders. `.dashboard-kpi-card` is already protected by an explicit border in `dashboard-refresh.css`.
